pcbkit 2

// ESP32-WROOM-32E-N4 (Espressif Systems): Wi-Fi 802.11b/g/n, Bluetooth classic and LE module,
// dual-core Xtensa LX6 240 MHz (ESP32-D0WD-V3), 4 MB flash, PCB antenna, 3.3 V, 18 x 25.5 mm with
// 38 castellated pads (the ESP32 DevKitC's module)
// Compiled from the part sheet `parts/ESP32_WROOM_32E.json` (`parts.create`); status: checked.
// Datasheet:
// https://www.espressif.com/sites/default/files/documentation/esp32-wroom-32e_esp32-wroom-32ue_datasheet_en.pdf
// (v2.1)
// Pins: Espressif ESP32-WROOM-32E & WROOM-32UE datasheet v2.1: table 3 pin definitions, figure 3
// pin layout, table 4 strapping pins, tables 13-14 ratings, figure 9 peripheral schematics, figure
// 10 dimensions and figure 13 land pattern
// Footprint: the datasheet's land pattern
// Symbol: digikey-kicad d4bd68f42e6ccc474526811a853a03692e170b58
// dk_RF-Transceiver-Modules:ESP32-WROOM-32 (CC-BY-SA-4.0),
// https://github.com/Digi-Key/digikey-kicad-library
// Parameters: digikey-kicad d4bd68f42e6ccc474526811a853a03692e170b58
// dk_RF-Transceiver-Modules:ESP32-WROOM-32 (CC-BY-SA-4.0),
// https://github.com/Digi-Key/digikey-kicad-library
// This file may be used, changed and shared without conditions, with the board or alone.

// Note: Supply: 3.0-3.6 V able to deliver 500 mA (Wi-Fi TX peaks); 22 uF and 100 nF at the 3V3
// pin.
// Note: Strapping pins sampled at reset: IO0 (pull-up; low = download), IO2 (pull-down), IO12 MTDI
// (pull-down; high breaks boot with 3.3 V flash), IO15 MTDO (pull-up), IO5 (pull-up). Do not load
// them so they read wrong at reset.
// Note: IO34, IO35, SENSOR_VP (GPIO36) and SENSOR_VN (GPIO39) are input only, without pull-ups.
// ADC2 is not usable while Wi-Fi runs: use ADC1 (IO32-IO39) for analog.
// Note: Antenna: the top 6.19 mm of the module. The footprint keeps tracks, vias, pours and other
// parts out of it (0.5 mm margin). Espressif's hardware design guidelines recommend the antenna
// outside the base board or at its edge with the board cut away under it, and 15 mm clearance
// around it: place the module at a board edge with the antenna overhanging it (`place =
// [edge(.top, overhang = 6mm)]`).
// Note: The EPAD (pin 39) to ground with thermal vias improves heat flow; it is optional, and too
// much paste lifts the module.

